  "arrangerNotes": "Verse 1 (Palm Sunday hymn), soprano (melody) line, verified against the Mutopia LilyPond score. 'Israel' is sung in three syllables; a slurred pair carries one syllable in 'comest'. No simplification needed. D drum: as written (range 1 to high 3), D minLayout 13. C drum: the C drum has no high 2/3, so line 2 ('to thee, Redeemer, King') and lines 4–5 ('made sweet hosannas ring. Thou art the King of Israel') are played one octave lower; C minLayout 11. C and D arrangements differ where noted above (each fits its own drum).",
  "verified": true
